[phase5/homepage-closeout 5bbac533c] [autopilot] UX08 deal of the day: Electro's countdown pill in the heading row, live's red corner badge on the photograph, a real add-to-cart that confirms in place, 12px corners. Measured before (logs/ux08/before.json, the existing build of HEAD at 380/768/1440 on 3346): the countdown was a 14px label beside a separate 4px-radius monospace chip (16px/900, 1.6px tracking) on its own row; the percentage was "50% הנחה" as a yellow chip with the 25px MODAL radius inline in the price row; the CTA was a link "לרכישה" to the product page; and the card and the photograph were rounded-lg, i.e. 25px (UX07 found the same on the category tiles). Now: DealCountdown is one brand-yellow full-round pill, 15px/700 in the heading colour, min 36 tall with 34px inline padding (--spacing-deal-countdown, --spacing-deal-countdown-pad; the size is --text-body-lg), "מסתיים בעוד: HH:MM:SS" with the figures in the body face and tabular-nums, 30px after the h2 on the same line and wrapped under it on a phone; the shape is Electro's .deal-countdown-timer off refs/electro-home-v7_computed.json (207x36, padding 5px 34px, radius 50px), since live has no countdown anywhere (live-home-sections.test.ts). The percentage is live's own deals-card badge (.p_con__badge: --color-deal-badge red, white 12/700, 4px corner, 2px 10px) pinned to the inline-end top corner of the photograph as "-50%", with the ltr on an INNER span because end-0 resolves against the element's own direction (with it on the badge the e2e measured the badge on the right corner, x 371 vs 162), and the percentage stays in the price row for a screen reader only; the span is on home-rtl.spec's LTR_ALLOWED. The CTA is AddToCartButton (product id, price in agorot, 44 tall) in the same yellow pill; AddToCartButton gains an optional addedLabel/addedClassName: after the store resolved TRUE (the same accepted the analytics wait for, never on a refusal) it sets data-added, appends the class and reads the label with a check for ADDED_CONFIRMATION_MS = 1800, timer cleared on unmount, every other caller unchanged. DealOfTheDay restyles that state through Tailwind v4 data-added: variants to --color-sale-badge with white (brand-contrast.test.ts refuses white on the yellow; the state string sits on its own line so the line-based gate does not read yellow and white together), and globals.css adds .deal-cta--added (deal-cta-pop 420ms on the header badge's curve, deal-cta-check on the svg); the global reduced-motion rule collapses both and the colour and label still read. The category link gets a 24px hit box (touch-targets.spec.ts measured 97x16). Measured after (logs/ux08/after.json): pill 226x36 yellow 15/700, centred on the title at 768/1440 (y 295.3 vs 296.8) and under it at 380; badge 47x28 red/white 4px at the photograph's own x and y; card and photograph 12px; CTA a 44px button; added-state.json: yellow -> rgb(50,134,20)/white, animation deal-cta-pop 0.42s, svg deal-cta-check, cart drawer open, reverted after 2.2s. Pinned by DealCountdown.test.tsx (3), DealOfTheDay.test.tsx (8), add-to-cart-added-state.test.tsx (6) and e2e/deal-of-the-day.spec.ts (6/6 chromium + mobile-chrome, which really adds and asserts dialog.cart-drawer[open] 0 -> 1). Neighbour e2e (home-rtl, touch-targets, a11y, home on both projects): 64 failing titles, byte-identical to UX06's set (comm empty, logs/ux08/failing-titles.txt); on / only the two prior offenders remain (input#masthead-search ltr, a[התחברות] 72x41). Measured: full suite 826 files / 9659 tests green, type-check and repo-wide lint clean, build green, home gate 2.22 / 1.24 / 1.32 against the frozen captures (unchanged; the section is below the 2600px the gate scores).
